# PLACEHOLDER — the Grow Lamp, an LED panel hung on copper chains.
#
# The model is a 14x3x14 copper panel (y 4..7) on two vanilla copper chains. Only three things are
# drawn here, and each face uses a region of its texture:
#   grow_lamp_top      the panel's top, uv 1..15 — vents over the driver
#   grow_lamp_side     the panel's edge, uv rows 0..2 — a copper band; lit, its lowest row is the
#                      diode strip glowing, so a powered lamp reads lit from the side too
#   grow_lamp_bottom   the diode array, uv 1..15 — dark violet off, UV violet lit
# The rest of each 16x16 is filler that only the break particles ever show.
#
# The diodes are the only purple there is: Minecraft light has no colour, so the lamp lights the
# world white like every other light source. Shifted from magenta to violet on 2026-09-15, to read
# as UV and blurple LED grow lights.
#
# It was a full copper cube until 2026-09-15, whose only lit face was the underside: a powered lamp
# looked unpowered from every other angle, and in daylight that read as "gives no light".
#
#   python3 .claude/skills/minecraft-texture-painter/scripts/mctex.py render \
#     textures-src/grow_lamp.mctex -o src/main/resources/assets/hempdustry/textures --preview

@palette default
a = 6D3421      copper, deep shadow
b = 8A4129
c = A4553A      copper mid
d = C0684C
e = D8845E      copper highlight
f = E9A07A
g = 2B1B2E      diode housing, dark
h = 3E2744
i = 3B2A66      diode off, dark violet
j = 4F3A85

@palette lit extends=default
i = 8A3CFF      diode lit — UV violet, the blurple of an LED grow light
j = CDB0FF      diode core, lavender hot spot

@matrix band 16x16
fefefefefefefefe
dcdcdcdcdcdcdcdc
hjhihjhihjhihjhi
dddddddddddddddd
dcccccccccccccca
dcdddddddddddddb
dcdcccccccccccdb
dcdcddddddddcdcb
dcdcddddddddcdcb
dcdcccccccccccdb
dcdddddddddddddb
dcdddddddddddddb
dcccccccccccccca
dddddddddddddddd
cccccccccccccccc
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbba

@texture block/grow_lamp_side from=band type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_side_on from=band palette=lit type=block

@texture block/grow_lamp_top 16x16 type=block
eeeeeeeeeeeeeeed
efffffffffffffdc
efddddddddddddcc
efdcccccccccccbc
efdcabababababbc
efdcccccccccccbc
efdcabababababbc
efdcccccccccccbc
efdcabababababbc
efdcccccccccccbc
efdcabababababbc
efdcccccccccccbc
efdbbbbbbbbbbbbc
efddddddddddddcc
edccccccccccccbb
dcbbbbbbbbbbbbba

@matrix diodes 16x16
dddddddddddddddd
dcccccccccccccca
dchhhhhhhhhhhhba
dchjihjihjihjhba
dchiihiihiihihba
dchhhhhhhhhhhhba
dchjihjihjihjhba
dchiihiihiihihba
dchhhhhhhhhhhhba
dchjihjihjihjhba
dchiihiihiihihba
dchhhhhhhhhhhhba
dchjihjihjihjhba
dchiihiihiihihba
dcbbbbbbbbbbbbba
daaaaaaaaaaaaaaa

@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom from=diodes type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom_on from=diodes palette=lit type=block

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LabPBR specular maps (_s), for shader packs set to resource-pack PBR (Complementary: RP_MODE
# labPBR). Same drawings, so every pixel lines up with its art. Per the LabPBR standard:
#   R  perceptual smoothness        G  F0, or 230-255 = a hardcoded metal — 234 is copper
#   B  porosity / SSS (0 here)      A  emission 0-254; 255 means "none" and is what non-glowing
#                                      pixels carry
# The copper housing is metal 234; the diode housing and lenses are a dielectric (G 10, ~4%).
# Lit, the diodes glow: lens 200, core 254 — which is what makes a LabPBR pack render them as a
# violet UV light. Nothing here can colour the light the lamp casts; see crops.md, the Grow Lamp.

@palette spec
a = 46EA00FF
b = 5AEA00FF
c = 6EEA00FF
d = 82EA00FF
e = 96EA00FF
f = AAEA00FF
g = 3C0A00FF
h = 460A00FF
i = C80A00FF
j = DC0A00FF

@palette spec_lit extends=spec
i = C80A00C8
j = DC0A00FE

@texture block/grow_lamp_side_s from=band palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_side_on_s from=band palette=spec_lit type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_top_s from=block/grow_lamp_top palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom_s from=diodes palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom_on_s from=diodes palette=spec_lit type=block
